.git/**
.gitignore
.claude/**
scratch/**
test/**
sample/**
tsconfig.json
.github/**
**/*.map
node_modules/@types/**
**/.DS_Store
*.vsix
# scripts/ ships (generate-library-signatures.ps1 is invoked by the Update Library Definitions
# command), so the dev-only scripts in it must be excluded — one by one for loose files, and by
# directory for the sub-folders the rest have been organised into.
scripts/build-vsix.sh
scripts/run-build.bat
scripts/install-vsix.bat
scripts/make-icon.js
scripts/Create sample PLC project/**
scripts/Build PLC project/**
# The only thing in the repo that talks to the internet. It regenerates a committed data file and is
# run by a developer by hand; shipping it inside an extension whose whole premise is being offline
# would be wrong even though nothing invokes it.
scripts/fetch-pragma-catalog.js
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md
DEVELOPMENT.md
# Implementation plans — developer working documents, same category as the three files above.
docs/**
# Agent working directory: briefs, diffs, review reports. It is git-IGNORED, which is exactly why it
# needs listing here — .gitignore has no effect on what vsce packages, so this shipped 1.12 MB of
# internal review material (including identifiers redacted out of the source) until it was caught.
.superpowers/**
